ords from the `refund` category, \"refund\" and \"charged\". The duplicate charge also relates to \"payment\". The keywords match directly, so the default category was not needed.\n\n## Routing Decision\n\nRoute to **Billing Support**, but only after eligibility and payment status are confirmed. The frozen policy says: *\"Check order eligibility and payment status. If eligible, route to billing support for refund processing.\"*\n\n## Policy Application\n\n1. **Check order eligibility.** This is pending because no order data was supplied.\n2. **Check payment status.** This is pending because no transaction records were supplied. We need to confirm whether two charges actually settled, or whether one was a pending or authorization hold.\n3. **If eligible, route to Billing Support for refund processing.** This step depends on steps 1 and 2.\n\n## Next Actions\n\n1. Check refund eligibility.\n2. Verify payment transaction status.\n3. Route to Billing Support if refund criteria are met.\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThe input does not include the following, so none of it is assumed:\n\n- **Order ID or account order history** for user_a. This is needed to check eligibility.\n- **Payment transaction records.** These are needed to confirm the duplicate charge. The relevant details are the transaction IDs, amounts, timestamps, and whether each charge is settled or pending.\n- **Charge amount(s) and payment method.**\n- **Refund eligibility criteria.** The policy says to \"check eligibility\" but gives no specific rules, such as time windows or conditions.\n- **Refund method or timeline** to tell the customer. The policy does not specify these.\n\nRefund eligibility cannot be confirmed until this information is obtained.","ttft_ms":1857,"type":"result","duration_ms":8409,"uuid":"b6559949-3027-42ac-83eb-1b58b10a099a","ttft_stream_ms":1387,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":1387,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
